From 00403c4fb59e2480abd2d9c9fe925b9fdf296d96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matterward Labs <admin@matterwardlabs.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:07:28 +0530
Subject: delete a marked ephemeral profile on Android

A restore that is abandoned before commit leaves a hidden ephemeral profile
that Chromium's Android profile lifecycle has no way to remove: the desktop
DeleteProfileHelper is not built here, and the ordinary Android deletion path
refuses a profile that is neither active nor last.

Add DeleteMarkedEphemeralProfileOnAndroid, a narrow physical continuation for
a caller that has already synchronized its own durable deletion authority and
written the kProfilesDeleted marker. It detaches and deletes; it never
regularizes or activates the profile, and a false result retains the marker as
evidence rather than as permission to retry.

Reconcile those markers once at startup. An interrupted deletion is identified
by the durable marker together with the persisted ephemeral bit; anything
unsafe or stale is forgotten without touching a filesystem path, and a
malformed dedicated marker fences every automatic deletion in that pass rather
than guessing which path it meant.

Declare the startup sweep in the header. It was defined with internal linkage
and called from profile_manager_unittest.cc, which is a separate translation
unit, so that reference could never have resolved.

Specified by
chromium/patches/0049-delete-a-marked-ephemeral-profile-on-android.md.

Taffy-Patch: 0049

